{"global_id": "medeasi_000001", "source_text": "Conjunctival redness, eye ache, foreign body sensation, photophobia, and lacrimation may be minimal initially.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 6.5, "ARI": 18.2, "FKGL": 15.8, "Dale-Chall": 13.35, "char_count": 110, "alphanum_count": 92, "word_count": 19, "sentence_count": 1}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "Corneal ulcers cause redness, pain, usually a feeling like a foreign object is in the eye (foreign body sensation), aching, sensitivity to bright light, and increased tear production.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 26.14, "ARI": 18.8, "FKGL": 16.6, "Dale-Chall": 11.23, "char_count": 183, "alphanum_count": 148, "word_count": 36, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 1.66, "word_compression_rate": 1.89, "sentence_compression_rate": 1.0, "BLEU": 6.280797907983447, "BERTScore": 0.8787745833396912}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000002", "source_text": "Desmopressin", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 36.62, "ARI": 35.6, "FKGL": 8.4, "Dale-Chall": 19.48, "char_count": 12, "alphanum_count": 12, "word_count": 1, "sentence_count": 1}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "Sometimes, the drug desmopressin", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 75.88, "ARI": 14.7, "FKGL": 3.7, "Dale-Chall": 11.73, "char_count": 32, "alphanum_count": 28, "word_count": 5, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 2.67, "word_compression_rate": 5.0, "sentence_compression_rate": 1.0, "BLEU": 0.0, "BERTScore": 0.8786365985870361}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000003", "source_text": "Frequency, urgency, and nocturia are due to incomplete emptying and rapid refilling of the bladder. Decreased size and force of the urinary stream cause hesitancy and intermittency. Pain and dysuria are usually not present. Sensations of incomplete emptying, terminal dribbling, overflow incontinence, or complete urinary retention may ensue.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 17.0, "ARI": 13.5, "FKGL": 13.9, "Dale-Chall": 11.8, "char_count": 342, "alphanum_count": 286, "word_count": 57, "sentence_count": 4}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "At first, men may have difficulty starting urination. Urination may also feel incomplete. Because the bladder does not empty completely, men have to urinate more frequently, often at night (nocturia).", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 52.87, "ARI": 10.4, "FKGL": 8.4, "Dale-Chall": 8.87, "char_count": 200, "alphanum_count": 163, "word_count": 38, "sentence_count": 3, "char_compression_rate": 0.58, "word_compression_rate": 0.67, "sentence_compression_rate": 0.75, "BLEU": 1.877055586770535, "BERTScore": 0.8572916388511658}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000004", "source_text": "However, if the neonate 's breathing appears obstructed, suctioning is done with an endotracheal tube attached to a meconium aspirator.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 25.8, "ARI": 15.9, "FKGL": 14.6, "Dale-Chall": 13.31, "char_count": 135, "alphanum_count": 112, "word_count": 23, "sentence_count": 1}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "If the newborn 's airway seems blocked by meconium, doctors try to suction it out. Doctors used to do suctioning whenever they saw meconium in the amniotic fluid or in the newborn 's mouth, but this has not been shown to help.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 67.08, "ARI": 9.8, "FKGL": 9.1, "Dale-Chall": 9.19, "char_count": 226, "alphanum_count": 179, "word_count": 46, "sentence_count": 2, "char_compression_rate": 1.67, "word_compression_rate": 2.0, "sentence_compression_rate": 2.0, "BLEU": 1.3366097779404034, "BERTScore": 0.8909732699394226}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000005", "source_text": "In the most severe form (called malignant yellow fever), delirium, intractable hiccups, seizures, coma, and multiple organ failure may occur terminally.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 16.32, "ARI": 18.7, "FKGL": 16.2, "Dale-Chall": 13.7, "char_count": 152, "alphanum_count": 124, "word_count": 29, "sentence_count": 1}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "Severe infection can cause seizures, malfunction of several organs, and coma may occur.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 41.36, "ARI": 12.2, "FKGL": 10.7, "Dale-Chall": 12.78, "char_count": 87, "alphanum_count": 72, "word_count": 16, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 0.57, "word_compression_rate": 0.55, "sentence_compression_rate": 1.0, "BLEU": 4.03966535471315, "BERTScore": 0.8964487314224243}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000006", "source_text": "Intervention for obese adolescents should be focused on developing healthy eating and exercise habits rather than on losing a specific amount of weight.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 22.75, "ARI": 16.7, "FKGL": 15.8, "Dale-Chall": 12.33, "char_count": 152, "alphanum_count": 129, "word_count": 24, "sentence_count": 1}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "The treatment of adolescent obesity is focused on developing healthy eating and exercise habits rather than on losing a specific amount of weight.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 22.75, "ARI": 15.5, "FKGL": 15.8, "Dale-Chall": 12.33, "char_count": 146, "alphanum_count": 123, "word_count": 24, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 0.96, "word_compression_rate": 1.0, "sentence_compression_rate": 1.0, "BLEU": 73.25510644096215, "BERTScore": 0.9702466130256653}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000007", "source_text": "Involvement of the carotid and vertebral arteries results in reduced cerebral blood flow manifested by dizziness, syncope, orthostatic hypotension, headaches, transient visual disturbances, transient ischemic attacks, or strokes. Stenotic lesions in a subclavian artery near the origin of a patent vertebral artery can cause posterior circulation ischemic neurologic symptoms or syncope when the arm is used (called subclavian steal syndrome).", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": -1.28, "ARI": 23.7, "FKGL": 20.9, "Dale-Chall": 13.28, "char_count": 443, "alphanum_count": 374, "word_count": 70, "sentence_count": 2}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "Head: People may feel dizzy or faint, have headaches, or have problems with vision.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 74.19, "ARI": 9.1, "FKGL": 6.4, "Dale-Chall": 8.84, "char_count": 83, "alphanum_count": 66, "word_count": 18, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 0.19, "word_compression_rate": 0.26, "sentence_compression_rate": 0.5, "BLEU": 0.37403405401475043, "BERTScore": 0.8440352082252502}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000008", "source_text": "Photosensitivity occurs in some patients. Lupus erythematosus tumidus is characterized by pink to violaceous urticarial nonscarring plaques and/or nodules, some annular, in light -exposed areas.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 8.03, "ARI": 16.8, "FKGL": 15.2, "Dale-Chall": 13.73, "char_count": 194, "alphanum_count": 164, "word_count": 29, "sentence_count": 2}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "Rashes resulting from exposure to sunlight (photosensitivity) occur in some people with lupus, particularly fair-skinned people.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": -3.99, "ARI": 19.8, "FKGL": 17.8, "Dale-Chall": 12.33, "char_count": 128, "alphanum_count": 108, "word_count": 20, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 0.66, "word_compression_rate": 0.69, "sentence_compression_rate": 0.5, "BLEU": 2.7779970710903115, "BERTScore": 0.8377863764762878}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000009", "source_text": "Recurrence rates after surgical excision are about 5 to 15 %.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 44.41, "ARI": 7.6, "FKGL": 9.6, "Dale-Chall": 13.61, "char_count": 61, "alphanum_count": 46, "word_count": 12, "sentence_count": 1}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "After surgical removal, ganglia return in about 5 to 15 % of people.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 42.38, "ARI": 6.6, "FKGL": 10.3, "Dale-Chall": 10.81, "char_count": 68, "alphanum_count": 50, "word_count": 15, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 1.11, "word_compression_rate": 1.25, "sentence_compression_rate": 1.0, "BLEU": 26.760322756637912, "BERTScore": 0.9174965620040894}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000010", "source_text": "Some patients have weight loss, rarely enough to become underweight. Anemia, glossitis, angular stomatitis, and aphthous ulcers are usually seen in these patients.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 25.96, "ARI": 13.2, "FKGL": 12.5, "Dale-Chall": 11.76, "char_count": 163, "alphanum_count": 135, "word_count": 29, "sentence_count": 2}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "Some people are undernourished, have mild weight loss and anemia, or have mouth sores and an inflamed tongue.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 70.13, "ARI": 11.6, "FKGL": 8.0, "Dale-Chall": 9.79, "char_count": 109, "alphanum_count": 89, "word_count": 21, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 0.67, "word_compression_rate": 0.72, "sentence_compression_rate": 0.5, "BLEU": 3.6142963951903533, "BERTScore": 0.8682994246482849}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000011", "source_text": "The liver may be enlarged, hard, or tender; massive hepatomegaly with easily palpable nodules signifies advanced disease.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 37.3, "ARI": 16.2, "FKGL": 12.3, "Dale-Chall": 13.77, "char_count": 121, "alphanum_count": 101, "word_count": 21, "sentence_count": 1}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "Typically, the liver is enlarged and hard. It may feel tender and often lumpy.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 72.83, "ARI": 3.9, "FKGL": 4.8, "Dale-Chall": 8.5, "char_count": 78, "alphanum_count": 62, "word_count": 17, "sentence_count": 2, "char_compression_rate": 0.64, "word_compression_rate": 0.81, "sentence_compression_rate": 2.0, "BLEU": 2.9399878112585656, "BERTScore": 0.9015978574752808}}]}
{"global_id": "medeasi_000012", "source_text": "The driving force for these reactions is often the entropic benefit of gaseous evolution ( e.g.", "metadata": {"dataset": "medeasi", "original_split": "train", "experiment_split": "", "domain": "medical", "language": "en", "annotation": "human", "level": "sentence"}, "source_metrics": {"FRE": 30.87, "ARI": 11.2, "FKGL": 12.7, "Dale-Chall": 13.85, "char_count": 95, "alphanum_count": 77, "word_count": 17, "sentence_count": 1}, "simplifications": [{"simplification_text": "The driving force for these reactions is often the entropic benefit of releasing a gas ( e.g.", "simplification_version": 1, "grade_level": -1, "control_attributes": {"LevSim": 0.0, "NbChar": 0.0}, "simplification_dimensions": {"linguistic": {"lexical": false, "syntactic": false}}, "target_metrics": {"FRE": 55.24, "ARI": 9.2, "FKGL": 9.5, "Dale-Chall": 12.33, "char_count": 93, "alphanum_count": 74, "word_count": 18, "sentence_count": 1, "char_compression_rate": 0.98, "word_compression_rate": 1.06, "sentence_compression_rate": 1.0, "BLEU": 74.83293841345241, "BERTScore": 0.966582179069519}}]}
